    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L02 INTRINSIC MOTIVATION (THE PASSION TEST)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-3, 8175-107\n\nCRITERIA\n- 8175-3 Demonstrate initiative and self-direction.\n    * Evidence of recognizing the importance of proactive, independent decision making\n    * Evidence of identifying workplace needs\n    * Evidence of completing tasks with minimal direct supervision\n    * Evidence of applying solutions\n- 8175-107 Identify personal skills and interests applicable to the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n    * Evidence of individual personal skills (e.g., leadership ability, problem-solving ability, organizational ability)\n    * Evidence of interests (e.g., sports, theater, music, physical fitness, recreational activities, volunteer activities)\n    * Evidence of networking with local business representatives\n    * Evidence of volunteering or working in sports, entertainment, and event industries to gauge one’s interest in the business of sports, entertainment, and events and to gain valuable work experience\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nThis is a participation grade.\n\n- Did they answer the question?\n- Is it school appropriate?\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work passes when it completes every part of the assignment above, in the student's own words, and shows evidence for each competency listed. Specific examples, not general statements. Work that skips a part, or restates the prompt without doing it, does not pass.",
    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: The Passion Test (Intrinsic Motivation)\n\nDescription:\n\nTo be successful in a high energy field like Sports and Entertainment Marketing, you need \"drive.\" But drive comes from two places: Extrinsic Motivation (money, grades, rewards) and Intrinsic Motivation (doing something because you love it). The most successful people build careers around things they are inherently motivated to do.\n\nThe Task:\n\nPlease answer the following question in 2 to 3 sentences:\n\nWhat is something that you do because you are inherently motivated to do it?\n\n- It can be related to any of your interests (sports, art, coding, organizing, helping people), but please keep it school appropriate.\n- Explain *why* you enjoy it.\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your response as a Text Entry."
