    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L22 MY CAUSE MY CLEATS (THE CAMPAIGN PITCH)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-1, 8175-50, 8175-87, 8175-93\n\nCRITERIA\n- 8175-1 Demonstrate creativity and innovation.\n    * Evidence of discussing the importance of creativity and innovation in the workplace\n    * Evidence of brainstorming and contributing ideas, strategies, and solutions\n    * Evidence of developing and/or improving products, services, or processes\n    * Evidence of identifying and allocating available resources\n- 8175-50 Develop presentation skills as a form of business communication.\n    * Evidence of eye contact\n    * Evidence of voice tone and projection\n    * Evidence of appropriate appearance\n    * Evidence of the use of vocabulary appropriate to the audience\n    * Evidence of body language\n    * Evidence of use of technology\n    * Evidence of use of visuals\n    * Evidence of engagement of audience\n    * Evidence of adjustments based on audience size\n- 8175-87 Explain sponsorship and endorsements as they relate to the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n    * Evidence of the definition of sponsorship\n    * Evidence of the definition of endorsement\n    * Evidence of the differences between sponsorship and endorsement\n    * Evidence of types of sponsorship (e.g., naming rights, signage, exclusivity)\n- 8175-93 Describe the elements of sports, entertainment, and event promotional campaigns.\n    * Evidence of event, product, or service\n    * Evidence of campaign objectives\n    * Evidence of target marketing\n    * Evidence of campaign activities and schedule\n    * Evidence of budget\n    * Evidence of key performance indicators (KPI)\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nUtilize a checklist approach.\n\n- Cleat design included?\n- Charity identified?\n- Fundraising idea included?\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work passes when it completes every part of the assignment above, in the student's own words, and shows evidence for each competency listed. Specific examples, not general statements. Work that skips a part, or restates the prompt without doing it, does not pass.",
    "promptText": "Title: Project: My Cause My Cleats (The Campaign Pitch)\n\nDescription:\n\nIt is your job to design the visuals and the strategy for the \"My Cause My Cleats\" campaign. You are not just designing a shoe; you are designing a message that needs to raise money and awareness.\n\nDeliverables:\n\nCreate a slide presentation (approx. 5 to 7 slides) that \"pitches\" your concept to the NFL.\n\n1. The Partners\n\n- Identify the Athlete and the Non Profit.\n- Explain the \"Why.\"\n\n2. The Strategy\n\n- Awareness: How will these cleats get attention?\n- Fundraising: Propose one specific idea to raise money.\n\n3. The Visuals\n\n- The Cleats: Insert a picture of your final cleat design.\n- The Merch: Create one promotional item that visually represents three brands at once: The Athlete, The Non Profit, and The NFL Team.\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your presentation file."
